<title>USA: Reunion unit Indiana plant hit by strike.</title>
<headline>Reunion unit Indiana plant hit by strike.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reunion Industries Inc said Wednesday that about 280 employees went on strike at the Lafayette, Ind.,-based Rostone division of its Oneida Rostone Corp unit.</p>
<p>It said the employees struck on Tuesday over differences involving wage increases and other benefits, which remain unresolved.</p>
<p>The striking employees are represented by the International Brotherhood of Electrical Workers, AFL-CIO, and were working under a collective bargaining agreement that expired March 2, it said.</p>
